From: FingerBrowser
Subject: [PATCH 0015] key audio noise on sample value to preserve duplicates

The offline-render audio noise (0007) perturbed every sample with a
position-sequential PRNG, giving each sample an independent nudge. That
destroyed the duplicate sample values a real render naturally has: measured
unique-sample count over a 5000-sample render jumped from ~4736 to a maxed-out
5000, which CreepJS surfaces as "unique" and a detector can read as an
all-samples-distinct signature no real audio produces.

Key the perturbation on each sample's value (hash the float bits) instead of
its position, so equal samples get equal noise and stay equal. The duplicate
structure is preserved (unique count back to ~4735) while the fingerprint still
shifts deterministically per profile -- distinct audioNoise seeds still produce
distinct sums. getChannelData still matches copyFromChannel.

Depends on: 0001-0014.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_fingerprint.h b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_fingerprint.h
index 859682d8f8..65df927715 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_fingerprint.h
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_fingerprint.h
@@ -187,10 +187,20 @@ inline void PerturbAudio(float* data, size_t count, uint32_t seed) {
   if (!data || !seed) {
     return;
   }
-  uint32_t state = seed;
+  // Key the perturbation on each sample's VALUE, not its position. A
+  // position-sequential PRNG gave every sample an independent nudge, which
+  // destroyed the duplicate sample values a real render naturally has: measured
+  // unique-sample count jumped from ~4736/5000 to a maxed-out 5000/5000, a
+  // signature detectors read (CreepJS reports it as "unique"). Hashing the
+  // sample value means equal samples get equal noise and stay equal, so the
+  // duplicate structure is preserved while the fingerprint still shifts
+  // deterministically per profile.
   for (size_t i = 0; i < count; ++i) {
-    const float unit =
-        static_cast<float>(NextRandom(state) & 0xFFFFu) / 65535.0f - 0.5f;
+    uint32_t bits = 0;
+    static_assert(sizeof(bits) == sizeof(float), "float must be 32-bit");
+    __builtin_memcpy(&bits, &data[i], sizeof(bits));
+    const uint32_t h = PixelHash(seed, static_cast<int32_t>(bits), 0);
+    const float unit = static_cast<float>(h & 0xFFFFu) / 65535.0f - 0.5f;
     data[i] += unit * 2e-7f;
   }
 }
